\bibitem [{Note1()}]{Note1}%
  \BibitemOpen
  \bibinfo {note} {We emphasize that a static fermion propagator with a moat
  form, i.e., a nonmonotonic $\protect \boldsymbol {p}$-dependence, is
  unrelated to the moat regime. A well-known example is BCS theory, where the
  fermion propagator has a minimum at the Fermi momentum for nonzero diquark
  gap \cite {Casalbuoni:2018haw}. While this can also lead to spatially
  modulated correlations, it is not connected to possible inhomogeneous phases.
  In fact, even correlations in a free Fermi gas show modulations with
  wavenumbers directly related to $p_F$. So this is a phenomenon unrelated to
  the phase structure.}\BibitemShut {Stop}%
